1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:07,934
Welcome to Miqat Al-Khaleej, the unified fleet operations and financial management platform.

2
00:00:08,284 --> 00:00:19,588
An integrated Saudi platform connecting vehicle inspections and official contracts with e-invoicing, accounting, and ZATCA tax compliance.

3
00:00:19,938 --> 00:00:30,666
In this guided tour, we will walk through every module, highlighting the streamlined financial suite and the new Unified Financial Exports Center.

4
00:00:31,566 --> 00:00:39,894
We begin with secure authentication backed by encrypted HTTP-only sessions and role-based permissions.

5
00:00:40,244 --> 00:00:50,348
The workspace opens to the Executive Dashboard, bringing together fleet KPIs, contracts, and daily trip readiness at a glance.

6
00:00:50,698 --> 00:00:59,098
At the top are the live Makkah clock and one-click shortcuts to create a contract, invoice, or expense.

7
00:00:59,448 --> 00:01:09,408
Interactive cards and charts track daily contract trends, trip categories, and vehicle document expiry alerts.

8
00:01:09,758 --> 00:01:19,622
The entire interface switches seamlessly between Arabic RTL and English LTR layouts, as well as light and dark themes.

9
00:01:20,522 --> 00:01:31,178
In the Fleet registry, managers monitor every vehicle, passenger capacity, and registration or insurance expiration dates.

10
00:01:31,528 --> 00:01:40,048
Next, the Daily Inspections module verifies vehicle safety and operational readiness before any trip departs.

11
00:01:40,398 --> 00:01:51,174
The shared 16-point safety checklist covers engine gauges, brakes, tyres, lighting, fire extinguisher, and first aid readiness.

12
00:01:51,524 --> 00:02:01,748
Approved inspections link automatically to official contracts and invoices, with instant WhatsApp PDF dispatch.

13
00:02:02,648 --> 00:02:10,952
In Official Contracts, dispatchers issue transport contracts specifying the customer, route, assigned captain, and vehicle.

14
00:02:11,302 --> 00:02:21,070
Opening a contract displays the full passenger manifest, approval controls, and the public QR verification link.

15
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:32,004
Contracts can be dispatched to the driver via WhatsApp, with return-trip cloning and optional driver or representative trip payouts.

16
00:02:32,354 --> 00:02:41,090
Meanwhile, drivers access a dedicated mobile-friendly Captain Portal isolated from back-office financial data.

17
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:50,656
From their portal, captains manage daily inspections, view active contracts, and track trip earnings, custody, and advances.

18
00:02:51,556 --> 00:03:01,468
The Customer directory maintains corporate agencies, hotels, and individual clients with VAT IDs and Saudi national addresses.

19
00:03:01,818 --> 00:03:10,386
Each customer profile includes a live ledger of contracts, issued invoices, collected payments, and remaining balance.

20
00:03:10,736 --> 00:03:20,168
The Staff & Representatives workspace manages driver and agent profiles, monthly payroll drafts, operating custody, and personal advances.

21
00:03:20,518 --> 00:03:29,494
Every entitlement and settlement balance is tracked to exact halala precision with downloadable staff statements.

22
00:03:30,394 --> 00:03:39,418
Now we enter the redesigned financial suite; the Invoices list now shows live collection status badges right on every row.

23
00:03:39,768 --> 00:03:49,584
At a glance, teams distinguish Paid, Partially Paid with remaining due balance, and Unpaid invoices.

24
00:03:49,934 --> 00:03:59,318
One-click payment status pills and collapsible This Month / This Quarter filters keep the toolbar calm and effortless.

25
00:03:59,668 --> 00:04:10,276
Secondary actions like Copy #, Credit/Debit Notes, and Archive live neatly inside the action menu while Record Payment stays prominent.

26
00:04:10,626 --> 00:04:19,746
Inside Invoice Details, a clean progress bar tracks collected amounts, allowing bank or cash payment recording in seconds.

27
00:04:20,646 --> 00:04:29,574
Creating a new invoice follows an intuitive four-stage wizard built for both non-accountants and finance specialists.

28
00:04:29,924 --> 00:04:40,100
Stage one selects the document type and Individual vs. Business customer profile, auto-filling data from linked contracts.

29
00:04:40,450 --> 00:04:48,922
Stage two captures trip origin, destination, service line description, and transport operational details.

30
00:04:49,272 --> 00:04:59,784
Stage three computes 15% standard or 0% VAT lines accurately while updating the live side summary card in real time.

31
00:05:00,134 --> 00:05:10,574
Finally, Review & Confirm validates balances, enables optional WhatsApp auto-send, and tucks ledger codes under an optional disclosure.

32
00:05:11,474 --> 00:05:21,218
Purchases & Expenses tracks fuel, maintenance, insurance, and fleet costs under the same unified period selector.

33
00:05:21,568 --> 00:05:31,648
Each supplier bill displays its live payment badge and an inline Pay Supplier button for deferred invoices.

34
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:41,790
When logging a new expense, linking a vehicle from the fleet dropdown feeds directly into per-vehicle profitability reports.

35
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:52,628
Users switch cleanly between Before-VAT and Includes-15% pricing, seeing net cost versus recoverable input VAT immediately.

36
00:05:52,978 --> 00:06:03,946
Clear payment cards replace raw account dropdowns, while ledger account codes and VAT dates stay neatly inside Accountant Details.

37
00:06:04,846 --> 00:06:15,142
The Accounting Hub organizes five focused workspaces inside a single-row, scrollable underline tab bar.

38
00:06:15,492 --> 00:06:25,692
Profits & Expenses leads with operating net income KPIs followed by a four-card snapshot of Cash, Receivables, Payables, and Net VAT.

39
00:06:26,042 --> 00:06:34,514
Clicking any balance card opens that account's full General Ledger statement directly.

40
00:06:34,864 --> 00:06:45,472
Vehicle profitability now highlights margin percentages, while the 7-column Trial Balance rests neatly inside a collapsible disclosure.

41
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:55,278
Inside Receipts & Payments, an instant searchable document combobox replaces tedious pagination dropdowns and shows due balances.

42
00:06:55,628 --> 00:07:06,068
Account Ledger adds six one-click quick account chips, and Journals tucks opening templates and advanced filters away neatly.

43
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:17,192
Chart of Accounts presents a clean hierarchical tree paired with a compact three-stat overview for posting and group accounts.

44
00:07:17,542 --> 00:07:28,054
On the ZATCA VAT Return screen, four focused KPI cards pair with an interactive Box 6 to Box 16 net tax formula bar.

45
00:07:28,404 --> 00:07:37,932
Clicking Box 14 or Box 15 in the equation jumps directly to Adjustments & Filing Settings below.

46
00:07:38,282 --> 00:07:47,690
The official Boxes 1–16 table provides one-click copy buttons formatted for direct entry on the ZATCA portal.

47
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:58,000
Manual Selection mode allows hand-picking specific invoices for independent tax scenarios with instant recalculation and export.

48
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:08,766
At the bottom, Supporting Documents, Adjustments, and Audit Warnings are consolidated into one crisp three-tab review panel.

49
00:08:09,666 --> 00:08:20,490
Now introducing the newest capability: the Unified Financial Exports Center, exporting every financial dataset from a single page.

50
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:33,416
Start with four one-click bundles: Complete Audit Pack, ZATCA VAT & Tax, Cash & Receivables, or Management & Fleet P&L.

51
00:08:33,766 --> 00:08:46,870
The Advanced Filters panel filters across 19 dimensions including payment status, expense category, vehicle plate, GL account, and min/max amount.

52
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:57,396
Users toggle any combination of the nine financial datasets and immediately see live matched counts and totals in the summary strip.

53
00:08:57,746 --> 00:09:09,266
Live Preview tabs let teams inspect matching records before downloading, strictly enforcing per-section RBAC permissions.

54
00:09:09,616 --> 00:09:21,088
Finally, pick Arabic or English output language and export the entire filtered bundle in one click as A4 PDF, Excel CSV, or JSON.

55
00:09:21,988 --> 00:09:31,852
We conclude with System Settings: company & IBAN banking profiles, alongside ZATCA Phase 2 EGS integration readiness.

56
00:09:32,202 --> 00:09:40,818
The WhatsApp Integration console manages connection QR status and automated contract, invoice, and inspection notifications.

57
00:09:41,168 --> 00:09:51,608
Super Administrators configure granular module permissions and presets to keep financial and operational roles secure.

58
00:09:51,958 --> 00:10:01,390
With this unified architecture, Miqat Al-Khaleej unites daily fleet efficiency, effortless finance workflows, and full tax compliance.

59
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:10,020
Thank you for watching, and we wish your team productive operations with Miqat Al-Khaleej.
